Two things a reader of the A-vs-C decision should take from that table. The concentration argument the ruling makes is **correct** — 30 against a next-largest of 10 is the ~3x gap it claims, even though neither number is the one it printed. And the residual after this document is **flat and thin**: 89 sites spread over 31 documents, 27 of which hold 5 or fewer. Whatever a per-document hand read costs in fixed overhead, only two or three more documents can amortise it at all.

